  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: cbc795acf92c1fb48bae236e4ba4d39f, type: 3}
  m_Name: Q05_Junction_Equilibrium
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::PNJunctionLab.AssessmentQuestion
  questionId: q05_eq_junc
  topic: 2
  topicTag: 3. P-N Junction Equilibrium
  shortSummaryLabel: Drift = Diffusion & Flat EF
  promptText: At thermal equilibrium (V = 0 V) across an unbiased P-N junction, how are the electric field, net current, and Fermi level configured?
  options:
  - Field points P -> N, diffusion exceeds drift, and EF steps vertically by qV0
  - Uncovered + donors (N) and - acceptors (P) form an N -> P field; drift balances diffusion (Inet = 0) and EF is flat
  - Mobile carriers vanish throughout both bulk P and N regions
  - Energy bands remain completely flat across the metallurgical boundary
  correctIndex: 1
  explanation: Diffusion uncovers fixed + donor ions (N side) and - acceptor ions (P side), creating an N -> P field. Drift cancels diffusion (Inet = 0), EF aligns flat, and bands bend by qV0.
  recommendedStation: Station 4
